# Wrenn and Six's emblem: "Instant and sorcery cards in your graveyard have retrace." (CR 702.81a)
# Embereth Shieldbreaker is a creature card in the graveyard; only its main characteristics exist there (CR 715.4),
# so its sorcery Adventure, Battle Display, is not an instant or sorcery card and gets no retrace. Chain Lightning is
# a sorcery card and is retraced by discarding a land.
#
# Wrenn comes down on turn 3 and ticks up each turn to 7 loyalty by turn 9. Holding eight cards at the end of turn 9
# puts Shieldbreaker in the graveyard by discarding to hand size. On turn 11 Chain Lightning is cast from hand, Wrenn
# goes to -7, and with an untapped Mountain and a land in hand, Shieldbreaker offers no cast at all from the graveyard
# while Chain Lightning is retraced (the Forest discarded) for 3 more. Bot2's Sol Ring is there so that Battle Display
# ("destroy target artifact") would have a target: without one it would go unoffered for that reason alone.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Forest
Wrenn and Six
Chain Lightning
Embereth Shieldbreaker
Mountain
Forest
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp
Sol Ring
Swamp x20

